polymorphism is made of two words.
poly- many
morphism- ways to represent

simply it means many ways to represent a single entity

🔍 Why are languages without polymorphism called Object-Based Languages?
Because:
They use objects and classes, so they are based on objects.
But they don’t fully follow OOP principles, especially polymorphism or inheritance.
Hence, they are not called Object-Oriented, but rather Object-Based.

✅ 1. Compile-Time Polymorphism (Static Polymorphism)
It is the type of polymorphism where the method call is resolved at compile time. It is achieved through method overloading or operator overloading.

✅ 2. Runtime Polymorphism (Dynamic Polymorphism)
It is the type of polymorphism where the method call is resolved at runtime. It is achieved through method overriding using inheritance.